          "ruleId": "CVE-2026-44250",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-44250 - Netty is a network application framework for development of protocol servers and clients. In netty-codec-redis prior to versions 4.1.135.Final and 4.2.15.Final, an attacker can cause DoS by sending a crafted Redis payload with deeply nested arrays. This forces the server to allocate a massive number of state objects and collections, leading to memory exhaustion and an OutOfMemoryError. Versions 4.1.135.Final and 4.2.15.Final patch the issue."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
